  "body": "### Summary\nFollow-ups of the Fable review of #1401 (LOT-161 step 1), non-blocking there: make the release script's safety tests run somewhere other than the operator's Mac, and tidy three details.\n\n### Scope\n- **CI**: `scripts/tests/test_release_script_safety.py` (18 tests, macOS-only: PlistBuddy, plutil) skips on the ubuntu `scripts/tests` job (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:79`). Cheapest: one step in the existing `App build + tests` macOS job, plus a spec line that a script-only change is tested on a Mac before review (that job does not run on script-only PRs).\n- `scripts/release-testflight.sh:333-334`: the run-time warning of the provisioning opt-in should also name the App ID registration (the spec does).\n- `:152-158`: a nested git repository inside the repo is seen as outside by `inside_repo`.\n- `HFR_CHANNEL` is optional: consider making it required in `--beta` mode.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- The safety tests run in CI on a PR that changes the script, or the spec states the manual rule; each detail fixed with a test.\n\nRefs #251, #1401.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
